#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/fi.rc -- Finnish (Finland), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "fi"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. Left to right, Latin script with the letters ä ö å. The tone is
// the one of Windows in Finnish: the reader is addressed in the singular (sinä), by the imperative
// ("Valitse", "Napsauta"); Finnish has no grammatical gender, so the voice of the author and of the
// reader need none (RULES 14). Quotes are the Finnish ”…” (both marks alike, as in Windows). No
// case ending is put on a substitution ({0}, {1}): the phrase is built so that the word before it
// carries the case ("näppäintä {1}", "versio {0}"). The key names stay in Latin letters, as the
// hotkey field prints them (RULES 4). The name of the program is not translated and is not
// inflected: a word with the case ending follows it ("Lang Switcher -ohjelman").
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Finnish — `[general] language = "fi"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
